From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:14:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] FFmpeg: keep draining a hardware decoder until it reaches EOF

During a drain (DVD_CODEC_CTRL_DRAIN) CDVDVideoCodecFFmpeg::GetPicture()
answered VC_BUFFER as soon as a hardware-decoded frame had been taken,
although the hardware may still be filling its queue, and the drain
could end before the last pictures of the stream came out. Answer
VC_NONE instead while draining, so VideoPlayer keeps asking until
FFmpeg and the hardware have both reached EOF. Outside a drain nothing
changes.

Applies to Kodi as LibreELEC patches it; needs nothing else from this
series. Split out of yblod-03 (the native Dolby Vision source), where it
was found; it is not specific to Dolby Vision.
---
 .../cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
index 34ba54e..d34d7d7 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVDVideoCodecFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -892,6 +892,10 @@ CDVDVideoCodec::VCReturn CDVDVideoCodecFFmpeg::GetPicture(VideoPicture* pVideoPi
         return VC_ERROR;
     }
 
+    // A decoded frame was consumed, but hardware may still be filling its queue.
+    // During drain, continue until FFmpeg and the hardware reach their EOFs.
+    if (ret == VC_BUFFER && (m_codecControlFlags & DVD_CODEC_CTRL_DRAIN))
+      return VC_NONE;
     return ret;
   }
   // process filters for sw decoding
